> uu is UUencoded (can I use UULite even though the file is not a graphic?)

.uu is for unix uudecode (use it (or something equiv.) to decode the file)

> Z stands for the Zip format.

.Z is for unix compress... Use unix's uncompress command (or even zcat)
(or equiv.) to decompress it.

> tar: I don't know what this is or how to convert it.
>

.tar is from unix's tar (tape archive).

Best way to do it (if on a unix machine is via:)

% uudecode Mac1.tar.Z.uu
% zcat Mac1.tar.Z | tar -xf -
%
or:
% uudecode Mac1.tar.Z.uu
% uncompress Mac1.tar.Z
% tar -xf Mac1.tar

